          %h4#the_happy_code The HaPPY code
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correction+code"} quantum error correction code
            (a class of such codes really, indexed by a “cutoff”
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
            by
            = succeed "-states" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            that defines it) exhibits a discretized form of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ryu-Takayanagi+formula"} Ryu-Takayanagi formula
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
          %p
            Concretely, the the HaPPY
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/code+subspace"} code subspace
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            formed by:
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/HaPPYCodeTesselation.jpg", :width => "440px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#Harlow18"} Harlow 18
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                picking a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+tensor"} perfect tensor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
                6;
            %li
              %p
                picking a finite cutoff of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pentagon"} pentagonal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tesselation"} tesselation
                of the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+plane"} hyperbolic plane
            %li
              %p
                regarding its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré dual
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
                in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite-dimensional vector spaces
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    assigning
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                    to each
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex"} vertex
                    at the center of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pentagons"} pentagons
                    (show in blue), with 5 of its indices contracted with its neighbours in the hyperbolic plane,
                %li
                  %p and its 6th uncontracted index remaining as an input (shown in red);
            %li
              %p regarding the uncontracted edges at the cutoff boundary as output (shown in white)
